Dear Niranjan,

How Your Portfolio Has Done Overall

Your portfolio has delivered a modest XIRR of 1.50% since you began investing in November 2023. With Rs.7.68 lakh invested, your current portfolio value stands at Rs.7.71 lakh, generating a gain of Rs.0.02 lakh. While the returns have been subdued, this performance reflects the challenging market conditions your equity funds have navigated over this period. Your diversified approach across 5 funds and 5 different AMCs provides a solid foundation for long-term wealth creation.

Your Equity Funds

Your equity allocation, representing 74% of your portfolio, has faced headwinds with all three funds underperforming their respective benchmarks. Franklin India Flexi Cap Fund has generated an XIRR of -1.98% against the NIFTY 500 TRI's 7.96%, while ICICI Prudential Large Cap Fund delivered 0.30% compared to NIFTY 100 TRI's 7.59%. Kotak Midcap Fund returned 0.31% versus the NIFTY Midcap 150 TRI's strong 11.18% performance. Despite the current underperformance, these funds span different market capitalizations, providing good diversification for potential recovery as market conditions improve.

Your Hybrid Funds

The Edelweiss Balanced Advantage Fund, comprising 23% of your portfolio, has delivered an XIRR of 1.39% since November 2023. This fund has provided better stability compared to your pure equity investments, demonstrating the value of its balanced approach. The fund's dynamic asset allocation strategy has helped cushion some of the volatility experienced in the equity markets during this period.

Your Other Funds

Your recent addition of Mirae Asset Gold Silver Passive FOF in September 2025 shows an impressive XIRR of 57.47%. However, since this investment is less than 12 months old, we'll need to wait for at least a full year to conduct a meaningful performance assessment. This small 2.6% allocation adds commodity exposure to diversify your portfolio further.

Key Observations

While your portfolio's current performance appears modest, it's important to remember that you're still in the early stages of your investment journey with just over two years invested. The underperformance of your equity funds against benchmarks suggests there may be room for review, though market cycles often reward patience. Your well-diversified approach across different fund categories and AMCs positions you well for long-term growth. Consider staying invested and reviewing performance trends over longer periods to make more informed decisions about any potential portfolio adjustments.
